Local setup:
1. Copy .env.example to .env and fill values locally.
2. Generate TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY with: openssl rand -base64 32
3. Generate SESSION_SECRET with: openssl rand -hex 48
4. Create a GitHub OAuth App with callback URL http://localhost:8787/auth/github/callback.
5. Start PostgreSQL, run npm install, then npm run dev.
Production secrets belong in the hosting provider secret manager, never GitHub or frontend build variables.
